summary:
Mr. Chen Jiageng's former residence is located at the back corner of jimei town, now No.149 Jiageng Road. It was built in 1918, bombed by Japanese planes in 1938, and then rebuilt. 
The former residence is a representative building with the characteristics of southern Fujian. It is a two-story building with an area of 4,000 square meters, with white stone walls and green tiles covering the roof; 
The bronze statue of Mr. Chen Jiageng stands in front of the Return Hall, and the inscription "Overseas Chinese Flag, National Glory" by Chairman Mao Zedong is engraved on the stone screen behind the bronze statue.

China Geological Museum has a collection of more than 550,000 geological specimens, covering all fields of geoscience. 
Among them, there are famous dinosaur fossils such as giant Shandong dragon and Chinese dragon bird at home and abroad, famous ancient human fossils such as Beijingers, Yuanmou people and caveman, and a large number of precious prehistoric biological fossils such as fish, birds and insects with scientific and ornamental value; 
There are the world's largest "Crystal King", giant fluorite calcite cluster specimens, exquisite mineral specimens with Chinese characteristics such as azurite, cinnabar, realgar, orpiment, scheelite and stibnite, as well as a number of national treasures such as a wide variety of gems and jade.
